npp (0.3.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Open a large file with one copy of it in memory instead of four: the file,
    the decoded text, the text with its line endings rewritten, and the buffer
    itself. A 131 MiB file peaked at 747 MB and now peaks at 324, which is also
    what it settles at.
  * Read files 64 KiB at a time, folding line endings and dropping a byte-order
    mark as the bytes arrive, so a file that needs no conversion is never copied
    whole. Slightly faster as well as smaller: 868 ms against 927 on that file.
  * Keep the row mapping only while something is wrapped or folded. With neither
    it said nothing but "row n is line n", at forty-one megabytes for a file of a
    million and a half lines.
  * Give the accessibility tree its first 64 KiB from the document rather than a
    copy of the whole file, which was 131 MB allocated per update on that file.

 -- Neko++ maintainers <npp@example.invalid>  Wed, 25 Nov 2026 21:55:47 +0100

npp (0.3.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Colour an apostrophe only where the language quotes with it: a Rust
    lifetime, Haskell's x', Julia's a' and a YAML don't are no longer the start
    of a string that painted the rest of the line and every line below it.
  * Colour the name a definition declares: fn, def, function and their
    spellings in the other languages open a function without being called, and
    a call written through type arguments, collect::<Vec<_>>(), is one again.
  * Colour a number only as far as it goes: a range like 4..end is a number,
    two dots and a name, instead of one number that swallowed the name after it.

 -- Neko++ maintainers <npp@example.invalid>  Wed, 25 Nov 2026 20:49:24 +0100

npp (0.3.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Keep a selection across Alt+Tab: the keystroke that made the window switch
    was delivered to the window after it got the focus back, and a Tab pressed
    it over the selection -- four spaces where the copied text had been.
  * Draw one frame when the window comes back to the front or regains the focus,
    and ask again 120 ms later when the surface reports itself occluded, so a
    window cannot keep a frame the editor has moved on from.
  * Draw a long line only as far as the pane shows, instead of shaping the rest
    of a line nobody can see.

 -- Neko++ maintainers <npp@example.invalid>  Tue, 24 Nov 2026 16:13:53 +0100

npp (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Finish the find bar: Notepad++'s search options on three rows, the dialog's
    ten buttons and both histories, the mark tab, and the replace row on Ctrl+H,
    with Enter acting the replacement.
  * Select the find field with Ctrl+A and paste into it instead of behind it.
  * Add Notepad++'s floating Search window, behind a Preference; the docked bar
    stays what Ctrl+F and Ctrl+H open.
  * Give the editor's own commands an API, headless and in the window, and let
    get_command answer to the names run_command takes.
  * Add Playground mode: a page of code with a kitten on it -- gravity and
    ledges, a rainbow trail, runs that take the text with them, a page that
    mends, a wall of furniture to climb, super jumps across the page, and a page
    rebuilt every three minutes in fireworks.

 -- Neko++ maintainers <npp@example.invalid>  Mon, 23 Nov 2026 16:52:18 +0100

npp (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Open several files at once: the portal's open dialog asks for a multiple
    selection, and the built-in browser takes Ctrl+click, Shift+click and
    Ctrl+A.
  * Store recent and session paths absolute, so an entry still names its file
    after a restart from another directory, and say so when the file has gone.
  * Size the minimap to the document instead of the pane.
  * Take the launcher's startup token, and end the startup sequence on the
    hand-off path: a window from a right click has the focus, and the file
    manager's pointer stops turning.
  * Scan the fonts and measure the text beside the graphics device: 282 ms from
    launch to a focused window becomes 235 ms.

 -- Neko++ maintainers <npp@example.invalid>  Sun, 22 Nov 2026 06:52:10 +0100

npp (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial packaging.
  * Ships the editor, a desktop entry, three icon sizes and a manual page.
  * The X11 and Wayland client libraries are declared as dependencies even
    though the binary does not link against them: winit loads them with
    dlopen, so dpkg-shlibdeps cannot see them.

